For Day 48, I worked on Secure Multi-User RAG using Spring AI.

The idea was simple: if multiple users are using the same RAG system, one user shouldn't be able to access another user's documents.

What I worked on
Added userId to document metadata
Used PGVector metadata filtering
Added similarity threshold for relevant results
Tested document isolation between users
Connected the retrieved context to Qwen for the final answer

The flow I implemented:

User
 ↓
Question + User ID
 ↓
PGVector
 ↓
Filter by User ID
 ↓
Relevant Documents
 ↓
Qwen
 ↓
Answer
My main takeaway

RAG isn't only about getting the right answer.

When multiple users are involved, making sure each user only gets the data they're allowed to access is equally important.

